I found a problem.
This will take all variables even it should not.


```js

const foo = {
    foo() {
        super.bar();
        const nested = {
            nesteedMethod() {
                super.foo();
            }
        };
    }
};


```


The variable for `super.bar();` will be injected into `nesteedMethod`.

To prevent this, you can preserve original variables like

```rust
fn visit_mut_block_stmt(&mut self, s: &mut BlockStmt) {
    let orig_vars = self.extra_var.take();

    s.visit_mut_children_with(self);

    // Prepend

    self.extra_var = orig_vars;
}

```
